  "answer": "You can implement OAuth2 password authentication with bearer tokens in FastAPI using the `OAuth2PasswordBearer` security scheme from the `fastapi.security` module. \n\n```python\nfrom fastapi import FastAPI\nfrom fastapi.security import OAuth2PasswordBearer, OAuth2PasswordRequestForm\n\napp = FastAPI()\n\noauth2_scheme = OAuth2PasswordBearer(tokenUrl=\"token\")\n\n@app.post(\"/token\")\nasync def login(form_data: OAuth2PasswordRequestForm = Depends()):\n    # your login logic here\n    return {\"access_token\": \"value\", \"token_type\": \"bearer\"}\n```\n\n[tutorial/security/oauth2-jwt-0]",
